# 13. OTP SECURITY

Implement the exact proof-based OTP approach.

Every fulfilment group must receive an OTP hash, irrespective of mode.

The raw OTP must never be placed in:
- Kafka messages.
- Outbox payloads.
- Logs.
- OpenSearch documents.
- Live-proof responses.

For otp_verified:

The admin submits the OTP in the request body.

The backend computes:

otp_proof = HMAC_SHA256(OTP_HASH_SECRET, "hash:" + submitted_code)

Only the proof is written into the outbox payload.

The consumer performs a constant-time comparison against the stored otp_hash.

Correct proof:
- Deliver the order.

Incorrect proof:
- Add an otp_failed timeline record.
- Do not deliver.

All three fulfilment modes must enforce OTP verification.

The customer's own SAMPLE DEMO OTP may be displayed only through the authorised order response while the group remains undelivered.

The admin demo OTP endpoint is admin-only.

Never log request bodies containing OTP values.

